============================================================================
THE ANCHOR'S HONEST PRECISION
============================================================================

  k                = 1.36461191
  M (recorded form)= 1576.4 GeV      [M_red e^(-1/(k a_c) - 3/2)]
  M (gap eq. exact)= 3152.7 GeV      [factor 2 NOT absorbed]
  4*pi*m_H         = 1573.9 +/- 2.1 GeV
  quoted agreement = 0.15%

[1] The sensitivities the file itself records
    d lnM/d lnk       = 33.47   (corpus: 33.47)
    d lnk/d lnalpha_c = -0.2301
    d lnM/d lnalpha_c = 25.77   (corpus: 25.8)

    So a 1% error anywhere in alpha_c becomes a 26% error in the anchor, and a
    1% error in k becomes 33%. The construction amplifies; it does not average.

[2] The ambiguities the file names, priced

    (i) The convention factor. 6d records two available conventions differing
        by exactly two: 1576 GeV against 3153 GeV. The recorded headline uses
        one of them. That is a factor 2 with no argument in the number itself.

    (ii) The 6f residual. Section 6e establishes the constituents are charged
         (compensated, not neutral), so some Standard Model running survives on
         top of Thomas-Fermi screening. Sizing it at the pairing scale:
           alpha(M_Z)     -> anchor x  5.58
           alpha ~ 3 TeV  -> anchor x  8.89

[3] The honest band

    lower edge (convention value, residual off) :    1576.4 GeV
    upper edge (exact convention x residual at M_Z):   17576.5 GeV
    span                                        : x11.2

    4*pi*m_H = 1573.9 GeV sits at the very BOTTOM of that band.
    Expressed as a fraction of the span, the target sits at -0.0% of the way up.

============================================================================
VERDICT
============================================================================

    THE CRITICISM IS CORRECT, and the corpus already contains its own correction --
    it simply is not propagated to the headline.

    The anchor is advertised as landing within 0.14% of 4*pi*m_H. But the file itself
    records a factor-2 convention ambiguity (6d) and, once 6e's charged constituents
    are taken seriously, a residual running worth a further x5.6 at the Z pole (6f).
    Composed, the honest band spans a factor of 11, from 1576 GeV to 17577 GeV.

    A quoted agreement of 0.14% against a band spanning a factor of 11 is not a
    precision result. It is the bottom edge of an order-of-magnitude range, and the
    two extra digits carry no information: with d lnM/d lnk = 33.5, reproducing
    1576.1 rather than 1576 requires k to eight digits, which no part of the physics
    supplies.

    WHAT SHOULD BE QUOTED: the anchor lands at the electroweak scale, within a factor
    of a few, with the direction of every named residual being adverse. That is a real
    and non-trivial statement -- a construction with no electroweak input landing
    within an order of magnitude of 4*pi*m_H is worth reporting. It is simply not a
    0.14% statement, and 6d's own words ("factor-of-a-few band") already say so.

    This does not change the physics. It changes what may honestly be claimed about it,
    which is the only thing this script was asked to decide.

